  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Promoting Accountability and Citizens Engagement (PACE)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Project Promoting Accountability and Citizens Engagement (PACE): Strengthening Women&apos;s Participation in Politics and Governance Phase III Project works to empower women within the Sixteen Districts of Sierra Leone to increase their participation in politics and governance at National Level. This project will consider two main outputs for success: O1: Outcome 1.2 Enhance Women&#x2019;s Voice and Agency through Women in Governance Networks in all Districts; 02: Outcome 2.3 Increase Women Participation in Political Governance for Social Self-determination. 
A multi-stakeholder approach is adopted to achieve outputs: i) work with women networks, female councillors and MPs to represent the voices of women and to drive changes through transforming institutions and processes, ii) strengthen and support women networks to mobilize women groups and their allies to work with a collective voice to ensure the inclusion of women in policy planning and implementation, iii) mobilize and educate men, women, and political parties leaders and members on gender and inclusion for effective participation in politics and governance by women, iv) partners with district/city councils, CSOs and line ministries to promote gender equality and women&apos;s participation in politics and governance: women in each of these governing structures will demand for change to create environments that are gender-sensitive; and integrate the&#xa0; media in significant activities on an ongoing basis to serve as a vital catalyst for the popularization and mobilization on gender issues at all level by reporting on injustice, inequality and providing the space and platform for women to be confidently empowered champions of their rights at National Level.</narrative>
  </description>
